Source-grounded limits:
logic.rs:4613-4656 receives at most one event per host/turn, and only records/schedules a matching generation with a sequence above the view cursor.
provider/mod.rs:212-217 returns None while the checkpoint side task owns the serial link.
client.rs:297-306 pops the oldest queued event before reading more socket bytes.
recovery.rs:111-132 holds burst notifications inside CrashLink until the release flag changes; that internal slot and the transport queues were not exported in this attempt.
The burst row has parsed/notified/target/page counters all zero, so it was not a started replay that merely stopped at a checkpoint. The physical location of its undelivered notification is unproven.
Other seats did parse: 575 of 967 have nonzero parsed bytes at failure. Retained replay-page count is 310 over the final 37.099s; the whole-run totals include the long admission ramp and must not be called the 90s post-release partition.
Maintenance is 33.683126694s in that retained interval; checkpoint RPC is 2.119062033s, overlapping the loop. No subphase sample proves which maintenance call dominates.
Fixture recovery.rs:225 creates a distinct swarm per seat; messaging/service.rs:1597-1606 ready() reconciles then queries every swarm, and :1633-1638 events() queries every swarm again. store/sqlite.rs:23/61-75 bounds the idle connection LRU to 64. This is a static candidate, not measured attribution.

